From: Pixelado Dev <350114043+pixeladodev@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Party menu: the screen handed to Pixelado Party for the in-game menu

With party.fd (Pixelado Party runs the engine as its child), the menu and the room's wait screen are Party's: the engine pauses, writes both panels into a memfd (PXF1), drops DRM master and says SCREEN released; Party draws and gives the screen back. Volume, brightness, the FPS counter, the local wireless page and the quit come back as CMD lines. No channel, or no answer in time: the engine's own menu (BananaDS's menu.c, with 0004), as before. The channel is always built in.

A menu key's release opens the menu only after its press was seen while the game had the screen (F's release, after its press closed Party's menu, opened it again: a loop), and the menu keys do nothing for 250 ms after a menu closed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
